      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `req \u003c min`, and we know `min` is a power of 2, then the first check `req \u0026 (min - 1)` will be true, so we can skip explicitly calling `std::max(req, min)` and just use `req` for either the aligned or unaligned case.\n\nIt\u0027s also probable that `req` is divisible by `min` but still a power of 2, so we should use `SkIsPow2(req)` to decide which alignment function to call.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2e659a781e4e390f93937935277e346b687c33ac",
